{"name":"Climbing Ivy","hex":"#58714a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"climbing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sport of climbing, ascending a wall or a rock or another object using available holds, generally with the safety of a rope and belayer.","Climb; ascent."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of climb"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climbing"},{"term":"ivy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several woody, climbing, or trailing evergreen plants of the genus Hedera.","Any similar plant of any genus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Climbing","blocks":[{"text":"Climbing is the activity of using one's hands, feet, or other parts of the body to ascend steep topographical objects that can range from the world's tallest mountains to small boulders. Climbing is done for locomotion, sporting recreation, for competition, and in trades that rely on ascension, such as construction and military operations. Climbing is done indoors and outdoors, on natural surfaces, and on artificial surfaces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/01ElCaballo_copy.jpg/330px-01ElCaballo_copy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climbing","wikidata":"Q22857"},{"title":"Hedera","blocks":[{"text":"Hedera, commonly called ivy, is a genus of 12–15 species of evergreen climbing or ground-creeping woody plants in the family Araliaceae, native to Western Europe, Central Europe, Southern Europe, Macaronesia, northwestern Africa and across central-southern Asia east to Japan and Taiwan. Several species are cultivated as climbing ornamentals, and the name ivy especially denotes common ivy, known in North America as \"English ivy\", which is frequently planted to clothe brick walls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg/330px-Hedera_algeriensis_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedera","wikidata":"Q26771"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg/250px-Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg/500px-Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg/250px-Robi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobi-Bosh-Alain-Robert.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg/250px-Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg/500px-Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg/250px-Midnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Lightning_yosemite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Crack_climbing_in_Indian_Creek%2C_Utah.jpg/250px-Crack_climbing_in_Indian_Creek%2C_Utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Crack_climbing_in_Indian_Creek%2C_Utah.jpg/500px-Crack_climbing_in_Indian_Creek%2C_Utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&